       "text": "I haven't entered this order. You've confirmed the dose, but you haven't given a clinical reason for it. 50 mg of amlodipine is 5 times the maximum labeled dose, and I can't find a basis for it in this patient. A single dose that size could cause profound, prolonged hypotension and shock, and amlodipine's long half-life of 30 to 50 hours means the effect would last for days.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily right now. If more blood pressure control is needed, the usual next steps are titrating to 10 mg or adding a second agent.\n- **Review the dose with your attending and pharmacy.** If you think there's a real reason for a dose above the labeled maximum, they can review it. Once it's been approved, tell me who approved it and why, and I'll reconsider with that documented in the order note.\n\nWhich would you like?"
